o0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4418e864ff2791659ba84caf1788c2ee84c4f1e2712376ab67f77d0266f56eda","event_uuid":"f5eb2f8e-8638-4a4b-85e7-7d82758231ae","position":{"commit_sha":"27c5a2ee653d642a5c4be09ecaa79a09e4c87a57","position":"1794535597439766615-f5eb2f8e-8638-4a4b-85e7-7d82758231ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify evidence (AC3): `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` in worktree nematode-followups at commit aa4879b50dd (Gerrit 3387 patch set 1), 2026-11-12 16:39-17:17 PST, exit code 0. Lint \"All checks passed!\"; import-convention \"3 passed\"; default tier \"21249 passed, 29 skipped, 19 warnings in 2076.13s\"; integration tier \"218 passed, 2 skipped in 148.76s\". Gerrit 3387: LLM-Review +1 (1 advisory: the truncation path's diagnostic is not separately tested), Verified +1 (Actions run 43343923750), 0 unresolved; merged as 42e9f847d72bfe12c81d8aded0f1d0b02c55208a at 2026-11-12 17:50 PST.\nAC1: the RED test test_a_budget_failure_keeps_the_sanitized_run_shape_diagnostic failed with KeyError 'requests' before the fix and passes after it. The other new tests pin existing behavior and pass: check_stop_reason/check_response stop_reason (5 cases), the `length` truncation, and DET advisory + provider_provenance on the agentic verdict. tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py passes in full (22). AC2: check_complexity_baseline.py --check reports new=0 increased=0.","timestamp":1794534652128139888},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 18:07 PST: CLOSED through the completion-verifier gate on Bedrock (AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock; a profile-less attempt failed because the AWS default profile is disabled) at 18:06 PST. Gerrit 3387 merged as 42e9f847d72. The 1 LLM-Review advisory (the truncation path's diagnostic not separately tested) is recorded here, not filed.","timestamp":1794535597439766615}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794461500904460016,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0687e110-a67e-4f52-94f7-324c35933ccd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f"},{"link_uuid":"a277ff9c-f376-4756-8107-d68776b39274","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa03-b879-ece3-4556"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit 3359 (the agentic verdict adapter, merged aed975de61c) received 5 non-blocking review findings that were not addressed before it landed:\n\n1. `_agentic_outcome` in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py` (~:376) builds a fresh `LLMOutcome` whose diagnostic is only `{\"exception_type\": ...}` for budget, tool-loop and truncation failures. That drops the run-shape `diagnostic` dict which `run_failure.interpret_failure` already attaches to `LLMBudgetExhaustedError` and `RunawayToolLoopError`, so an operator reading a failed agentic verdict loses the step and call counts.\n2. The comment above the pipeline-only post-dispatch tail in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (~:624) still lists \"interim\" agentic verdicts, which no longer exist.\n3. No test checks that production `structured.check_stop_reason` sets `UnretryableOutputError.stop_reason`; the failure-class tests set it by hand.\n4. No test checks that a DET advisory finding and the agent call's `provider_provenance` reach the adapted agentic verdict through `gates/plan-review.yaml`.\n5. The truncation failure-class table covers `max_tokens` but not `length`.\n\n## Approach\n\n- In `_agentic_outcome`'s `fixed(...)` helper, build the diagnostic as `failure.sanitize_diagnostic({\"exception_type\": type(exc).__name__, **dict(getattr(exc, \"diagnostic\", {}) or {})})`. `sanitize_diagnostic` (`src/rebar/llm/failure.py:120`) is the existing allowlist + redactor every other outcome diagnostic goes through: it keeps only `_ALLOWED_FIELDS`, which already include the run-shape counters `usage_log.run_shape` writes that operators need (`requests`, `tool_calls`, `request_limit`, `tool_calls_limit`, `finish_reason`). Other run-shape keys (token counts, repetition summary) are dropped, as for every other outcome; `failure.py` is not changed.\n- Rewrite the comment to name the current agentic verdict kinds: floor, adapted and degraded.\n- Add tests:\n  - in `tests/unit/test_structured.py`, `check_stop_reason(\"refusal\")` and a `check_response` whose `provider_details` carries a `\"refusal\"` key each raise `UnretryableOutputError` with `stop_reason` set (`\"refusal\"`);\n  - in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`:\n    - a plan whose Layer-1 floor yields an advisory (e.g. empty `file_impact` → P9) reviewed under `engine=\"agentic\"` carries that DET advisory in `advisory`, and the verdict's `provider_provenance` equals what the fake runner stamped;\n    - a `length` truncation classifies as `CHANGE_SETTINGS`;\n    - an `LLMBudgetExhaustedError` carrying `diagnostic={\"requests\": 41, \"tool_calls\": 80, \"input_tokens\": 9}` yields a verdict whose `coverage.diagnostic` has `requests == 41` and `tool_calls == 80` and no `input_tokens`.\n\nNo new config key, flag or env var; no change to any verdict string.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (comment only)\n- tests/unit/test_structured.py\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The 4 new tests above pass, and `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py` passes in full.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py","reason":"carry sanitized run diagnostic"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"stale comment"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_structured.py","reason":"stop_reason stamping tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py","reason":"DET advisory, provenance, length, diagnostic tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","aa03-b879-ece3-4556"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"4cad8f86-e46a-4d78-b906-e9a3b67a666b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f04a-6819-c968-4826","ticket_type":"task","title":"Agentic adapter follow-ups from change 3359 review","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["28c440a1-7157-4cd2-84d0-a66c09291540","a835dac1-5335-4c04-97ea-ca8734eb8395","9de35e14-e094-4dec-939c-965261861ce1","c159c116-4ed0-4de6-984b-2cf22f026d89","62057949-e012-4d10-a644-e4e49ea03923","baf1ea8e-4cc9-4eff-9c3b-e1888197ef4c","969c3e5a-0a52-4727-a76b-83e45c2dd767","a277ff9c-f376-4756-8107-d68776b39274","a395f75c-fc2b-4f78-87f6-4eaa8c199fa3","d575eb87-f363-48e8-b544-182abf589d1e","4cad8f86-e46a-4d78-b906-e9a3b67a666b","9fd5fc14-c277-4521-9404-9352e9a94658","f5eb2f8e-8638-4a4b-85e7-7d82758231ae"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794535597439766616,"uuid":"5a041761-5406-4352-b08c-460eef3586fc"}